The condition is $d_{D-1} > d_i$ for all $0 \le i \le D-2$.
This implies $d_{D-1} > \max(d_{D-2}, \dots, d_0)$.
Also, since $d_{D-1}$ is the MSD, $d_{D-1} \in \{1, \dots, 9\}$.
The other digits $d_i$ can be any digit from $0$ to 9.
However, for the condition to hold, all $d_i$ (where $i < D-1$) must be strictly less than $d_{D-1}$.

